think Picked up the thread. Read KYRI + RADIANT_STYLE to be Kyri, then crux/REMEMBER, REDS, and the top session-log recommends. Standfast clear: every living REDS row CLOSED or Released, only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (deep-debride, not agent-closable). So reds-first satisfied, take the next constructive lap.
think Last lap was a REMEMBER condense at the roundness-quest / Season-G-media completion boundary; the roundness family is COMPLETE (inner exact, outer exact, universal proof). The card and recent logs named the next crux-first agent-doable rung as a further scene read; the Microkernel double-seat study rung sits behind a fetch/license gate (seL4 GPLv2 / Genode AGPLv3), surfaced not crossed.
think The scene-read family builds a surface's interaction floor: scene_manifest enumerates every object, hit_test names the ONE object under a POINT. The crux-first next rung is region_select -- name EVERY object a query RECTANGLE covers, the marquee / drag-select and crop-region primitive. It carries hit_test's box-is-a-prefilter crux ONE DIMENSION UP: an object's bounding box can overlap the rectangle while the object places no pixel there (an L's concavity, a ring's hole), so the box is a prefilter that over-counts and the label map is the arbiter.
think Designed the API compose-not-braid over label (the at arbiter), scene_manifest (ObjectEntry rows), regions (the box): QueryRect (inclusive corners), bbox_overlaps_rect (the prefilter), bbox_overlap_count (candidate count, over-counts the truth), select_in_rect (the arbiter -- scans the rectangle CLAMPED to the map, a presence tally per dense label, collects ascending, empty for background/off-map), is_selected. A malformed rectangle refuses BadRect; an off-map marquee is a valid EMPTY selection (a drag past the edge legitimately selects what lies under its on-map part), never a refusal.
think Hand-verified every fixture before coding on the L-and-block scene hit_test uses: a rectangle tight on the block (3,2)-(4,3) overlaps BOTH boxes (candidate 2) yet selects only the block; a rectangle in the empty concavity (column x=2) overlaps the L's box (candidate 1) yet selects nothing; a rectangle in a 5x5 ring's hole (2,2)-(4,4) sits in the ring's box (candidate 1) yet selects empty while a wall-crossing rectangle selects the ring; whole-scene selects both ascending; overhang clamps and selects; malformed refuses BadRect; determinism. Every value confirmed by hand first.
